WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:01.900
And where are you right now, Michael?

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:02.890
I'm in Reno, Nevada.

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:04.840
Okay, are you at a blackjack table?

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.375
Where are you specifically?

00:00:06.375 --> 00:00:07.378
(Sona laughing)

00:00:07.378 --> 00:00:08.300
I'm in my office, actually.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.910
I'm a consultant and a beverage educator.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.260
I'm a spirits educator,
so I'm in my office

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.070
where I take most of my Zoom calls.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:16.330
Oh, that's so funny,

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:17.940
'cause I heard that
you were a spirit guide

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.910
before you got on and I'm
realizing, I swear to god,

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.920
I thought you were a spirit guide.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.900
You're a spirits guide.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.530
You're a spirits educator.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:27.663
The S is very important.

00:00:27.663 --> 00:00:30.170
Yeah, because I'm sure there
are people that come to you

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.470
and say, can you help me find my,

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:35.140
I want to talk to my
great-grandfather and you say,

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.700
I can't do that, but I have
a really good port for you

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.960
that you might want to drink.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.490
I do a fair amount of
necromancy, but not a great deal.

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:44.500
Like I try to limit the amount.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.021
Man, here's another
thing, he says necromancy.

00:00:48.021 --> 00:00:49.130
I know.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:49.963
I love it.

00:00:49.963 --> 00:00:51.740
I love anyone who knows
that word and says,

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.370
I am a necromancer.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.760
It's such a menacing word
that no one uses anymore.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.840
Lots of drama in that word.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.870
Michael, tell me about this.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:01.140
I'm interested in this.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.800
You work with spirits.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.230
What does that mean exactly?

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:08.230
Do you help develop types of drinks

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.910
or do you mostly do you study drinks?

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:11.743
What do you do?

00:01:11.743 --> 00:01:13.087
All of it.

00:01:13.087 --> 00:01:14.910
So my principle job is
as a spirits educator

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:17.530
is to talk and teach and
get people into products,

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.330
teach people new things about drinks.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.500
I do beverage design for like menus.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.530
I design bars.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.040
And then my like full-time job I work

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.143
for a bartender advocacy agency,

00:01:26.143 --> 00:01:29.361
which is like a PR firm
specifically for bartenders.

00:01:29.361 --> 00:01:30.194
Whoa.

00:01:30.194 --> 00:01:31.027
That's fascinating.

00:01:31.027 --> 00:01:33.490
Now why do people need, I
mean, most people figure out

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.570
drinking pretty much
on their own, you know?

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:38.780
Don't you think most
people are self-taught

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:40.180
when it comes to alcohol.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.770
They figure out what they like to drink

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:44.570
and then they have way too
much of it and they get sick.

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:49.150
What do you find that you're
teaching people about?

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:52.160
Sort of more of the refined
aspects of certain spirits?

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:53.590
I always say I'm the Sherpa

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:55.415
up the mountain of alcohol, right?

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:56.567
(Sona laughing)

00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:59.874
So my job is to help you find
your new favorite friend.

00:01:59.874 --> 00:02:00.707
(Conan laughing)

00:02:00.707 --> 00:02:03.420
Okay, and what are your favorite drinks?

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.050
What drinks do you?

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:06.670
Tell us, what do you,

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:09.470
what's your favorite drink
that you find yourself

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:10.760
moving towards in life?

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:12.090
I mean, I love a piña colada.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:12.923
I love rum.

00:02:12.923 --> 00:02:15.840
So I like a piña colada
'cause they're fun.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.960
Who doesn't want a piña colada?

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.180
But I love bourbon.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:22.160
I help host a bourbon summer
camp that bartenders go to,

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.066
which is its own magical thing itself.

00:02:24.066 --> 00:02:24.899
What?

00:02:24.899 --> 00:02:26.220
A bourbon summer camp.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.223
Yes.

00:02:27.223 --> 00:02:29.090
This sounds so much better
than Craggett Mountain Farm,

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.990
where my parents sent me,

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:33.070
where there are peanut
butter and jelly sandwiches

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:35.630
and we had to climb the entire
Presidential Mountain Range

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:38.800
in July in New Hampshire
and be eaten to death

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.443
by mosquitoes and no one had invented

00:02:43.443 --> 00:02:46.210
any kind of sun lotion
yet, so I just burned up

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:48.400
and became a massive pustule.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:53.110
What you just described is a
much better camp, a rum camp.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:53.943
It's bourbon.

00:02:53.943 --> 00:02:55.263
Oh, bourbon, okay.

00:02:55.263 --> 00:02:56.120
Whatever, it doesn't matter.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.863
I'm gonna tell you something.

00:02:57.863 --> 00:02:59.220
I have a huge fondness for rum.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:03.230
I really do like rum and I like rum

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:05.250
in kind of a fruity punch.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.400
And I'm probably not
supposed to admit that,

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:11.200
but I do like a fruity rummy drink,

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.620
or like a rum punch, a
planter's punch, if you will.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.090
Why can't you admit that?

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:18.010
Because I also like it
when it has fruit in it

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:20.940
floating around and I like it when there's

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.346
like a little plastic statue in it too

00:03:23.346 --> 00:03:26.340
that's on the top of a swizzle stick.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:30.180
I like it to be a drink that
emasculates me immediately

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.390
the minute it's brought to my table,

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:32.530
those are my favorite drinks.

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:33.863
Big twisty straw.

00:03:33.863 --> 00:03:35.550
I like a twisty straw.

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:36.883
I love all that stuff.

